.TH CH-ADDS 1 "September 2026" "ch-adds 1.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ch-adds \- show only added lines from a file diff
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ch-adds
.I file
[\fIreference\fR]
[\fIoptions\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ch-adds
prints only added lines (\fB+\fR) from a unified diff, without context or removed
lines. It is a focused viewer for "what did I add in this file?" — not a
replacement for \fBgit diff\fR.
.PP
By default it compares the working tree and staged changes against \fBHEAD\fR.
.SH REFERENCES
.TP
.B HEAD
Working tree + staged vs last commit.
.TP
\fIcommit\fR, \fItag\fR
\fBgit diff\fR \fIref\fR \fB\-\-\fR \fIfile\fR when \fB\-\-exact\fR is used; otherwise
\fIref\fR...\fBHEAD\fR (3-dot, merge-request style).
.TP
\fIbranch\fR..\fBHEAD\fR, \fIbranch\fR...\fBHEAD\fR
Explicit git revision ranges.
.TP
\fIfile.patch\fR
Extract added lines for \fIfile\fR from a patch file (\fB\-p\fR).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-ref " \fIREF\fR
Reference (same semantics as the optional second argument).
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-patch " \fIFILE\fR
Read from a patch file instead of git. Use \fB\-\fR for stdin.
.TP
.B \-\-staged
Only staged changes (\fBgit diff \-\-cached\fR).
.TP
.B \-\-unstaged
Only unstaged changes (\fBgit diff\fR without \fB\-\-cached\fR).
.TP
.BR \-2 ", " \-\-two-dot
With a branch name, use \fIbranch\fR..\fBHEAD\fR instead of 3-dot.
.TP
.BR \-x ", " \-\-exact
Diff directly against \fIREF\fR (single tree).
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Print only added lines (no header or line numbers).
.TP
.BR \-0 ", " \-\-plain
With \fB\-q\fR, omit the leading \fB+\fR/\fB\-\fR on each line.
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-removed
Also show removed lines (\fB\-\fR), in unified-diff order. Removals use the
old-file line number and red highlighting; additions stay green.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show usage and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Show version, license, and source URL.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
When set, disable ANSI color output.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
ch-adds src/main.c
ch-adds k8s/pre/all/values.yaml develop
ch-adds src/main.c --staged
ch-adds src/main.c -p series.patch
ch-adds src/main.c develop -q | xclip -selection clipboard
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR git-diff (1)
